(7838895, 1313586, 100831, '<td valign="top">
There was once a man who learned to jump, higher than anyone thought possible. One day he catapulted himself up into the sky, higher and higher he went.. until he found himself swept up by a cloud of dust. He was carried for quite sometime before the dust descended and he was deposited onto a barren land, covered in black sand. As he landed, the sand began to shake, and pulse and then he was picked up again ... as if the clouds were a magic carpet. He looked back to see where he had landed but couldn''t tell. He tried holding his breath and counting backwards from 100 and it worked.... He was gently set back on earth, left wondering what had happened. Was it a dream or are we now closer to finding life on another planet?</td>', 'There was once a man who learned to jump, higher than anyone thought possible. One day he catapulted himself up into the sky, higher and higher he went.. until he found himself swept up by a cloud of dust. He was carried for quite sometime before the dust descended and he was deposited onto a barren land, covered in black sand. As he landed, the sand began to shake, and pulse and then he was picked up again ... as if the clouds were a magic carpet. He looked back to see where he had landed but couldn''t tell. He tried holding his breath and counting backwards from 100 and it worked.... He was gently set back on earth, left wondering what had happened. Was it a dream or are we now closer to finding life on another planet?', '2026-09-29 19:50:06.000000', NULL, 1),
