<br/>"Choose your course," he said, grinning.
<br/>She and her boyfriend laughed. They weren''t boaters. They were here to fish. 
<br/>"I''m serious," he said. "I''ve been doing fishing tours for 30 years. I''m going to be 70 next week. I''m tired. I''m bored. We could sail back to land, we could wander into perfect fishing, we could go so far into the sea we''ll run out of supplies. It all depends on which way you choose."
<br/>"But we... we don''t know where we are..." said Sarah.
<br/>"All I see is ocean," said her boyfriend.
<br/>"That''s ok," said the guide, grinning again. "You can just point. We''ll go in that direction."
<br/>"What if we don''t point?" asked Sarah.
<br/>The guide laughed loudly. "Then I''ll jump off this boat right now!"
<br/>The sun was directly above them. She couldn''t even figure out the cardinal directions. She stretched out her left hand and... pointed to a horizon that looked like every other horizon.
<br/>"And away we go!"</td>', 'Sarah was surprised at how quickly the land disappeared behind them. Their guide had just enough time to finish a sandwich.
"Choose your course," he said, grinning.
She and her boyfriend laughed. They weren''t boaters. They were here to fish. 
"I''m serious," he said. "I''ve been doing fishing tours for 30 years. I''m going to be 70 next week. I''m tired. I''m bored. We could sail back to land, we could wander into perfect fishing, we could go so far into the sea we''ll run out of supplies. It all depends on which way you choose."
"But we... we don''t know where we are..." said Sarah.
"All I see is ocean," said her boyfriend.
"That''s ok," said the guide, grinning again. "You can just point. We''ll go in that direction."
"What if we don''t point?" asked Sarah.
The guide laughed loudly. "Then I''ll jump off this boat right now!"
The sun was directly above them. She couldn''t even figure out the cardinal directions. She stretched out her left hand and... pointed to a horizon that looked like every other horizon.
"And away we go!"', '2026-09-29 23:09:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7839055, 1313598, 50695, '<td valign="top">
Bergman loved to fish. One day after a long, grueling shift at the tomato peeling yard, he showed up at his local stream with a backpack, long tangles of string, and hope. He noticed the flies that were buzzing around and knotted the grass in imitation, dancing his creations on the water''s surface. A giant catfish took one of of his fantasies, and his entire hand, in its mouth, pulling him into the cold water. 
<br/>
<br/>Bergman was reminded of his last performance review, how his boss seemed to inhabit a completely different world behind his desk, and everything he was saying only applied to that world, a world that Bergman didn''t know or understand. Nor could he understand it because he didn''t experience it. 
<br/>
<br/>But the catfish was different. The catfish was trying to show him its world, which  his elbow now understood completely. 
<br/>
<br/>"Will I be back in time for dinner?" asked Bergman. There was no answer, but he decided to go anyway.</td>', 'Bergman loved to fish. One day after a long, grueling shift at the tomato peeling yard, he showed up at his local stream with a backpack, long tangles of string, and hope. He noticed the flies that were buzzing around and knotted the grass in imitation, dancing his creations on the water''s surface. A giant catfish took one of of his fantasies, and his entire hand, in its mouth, pulling him into the cold water. 

Bergman was reminded of his last performance review, how his boss seemed to inhabit a completely different world behind his desk, and everything he was saying only applied to that world, a world that Bergman didn''t know or understand. Nor could he understand it because he didn''t experience it. 

But the catfish was different. The catfish was trying to show him its world, which  his elbow now understood completely. 

"Will I be back in time for dinner?" asked Bergman. There was no answer, but he decided to go anyway.', '2026-09-30 09:39:18.000000', NULL, 1),
